(   4. Civil Engineering Design & Stability Implications:) Tj
T*
(   Compression members must be checked for Euler column buckling \(P_cr = pi^2 * E * I / L_eff^2\),) Tj
T*
(   while tension members are governed by net cross-sectional yield strength under bridge/roof) Tj
T*
(   design standards.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove the three formal engineering rules for identifying Zero-Force Members in planar trusses by visual inspection.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Context & Equilibrium Classification:) Tj
T*
(   This analysis addresses internal member forces and structural determinacy for plane truss) Tj
T*
(   systems.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria: All joints are frictionless spherical pins; loads act exclusively at nodes;) Tj
T*
(   members are ideal two-force axial elements carrying pure tension \(+T\) or compression \(-C\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation & Step-by-Step Joint/Section Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Identification of Zero-Force Members by Visual Inspection:) Tj
T*
(   Zero-force members carry no axial force under a specific loading condition. Identifying them) Tj
T*
(   immediately simplifies truss analysis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Rule 1: Two Non-Collinear Members at an Unloaded Joint:) Tj
T*
(   - Statement: If only two non-collinear members meet at a joint where no external active load or) Tj
T*
(   support reaction acts, the axial force in both members MUST be zero.) Tj
T*
(   - Proof:) Tj
T*
(   Let members 1 and 2 meet at joint A at angle theta != 0.) Tj
T*
(   Align Cartesian axis x along member 1 and axis y perpendicular to member 1.) Tj
T*
(   Apply equilibrium in y-direction: Sigma Fy = 0:) Tj
T*
(   F2 * sin\(theta\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Since theta != 0 and sin\(theta\) != 0 => F2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Apply equilibrium in x-direction: Sigma Fx = 0:) Tj
T*
(   F1 + F2 * cos\(theta\) = 0 => F1 + 0 = 0 => F1 = 0. \(Proved\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Rule 2: Three Members at an Unloaded Joint with Two Collinear:) Tj
T*
(   - Statement: If three members meet at an unloaded joint where two of the members are collinear,) Tj
T*
(   the force in the third non-collinear member MUST be zero.) Tj
T*
(   - Proof:) Tj
T*
(   Let members 1 and 2 be collinear along the x-axis. Let member 3 meet at angle theta to the) Tj
T*
(   x-axis.) Tj
T*
(   Apply equilibrium perpendicular to the collinear axis \(y-axis\): Sigma Fy = 0:) Tj
T*
(   F3 * sin\(theta\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Since theta != 0 and sin\(theta\) != 0 => F3 = 0. \(Proved\)) Tj
T*
(   Furthermore: Sigma Fx = 0 => F1 + F2 = 0 => F1 = - F2 \(the two collinear members carry equal) Tj
T*
(   forces of opposite sense\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Rule 3: Two Non-Collinear Members with an External Force Collinear to One:) Tj
T*
(   - Statement: If two non-collinear members meet at a joint with an external load P collinear) Tj
T*
(   with member 1, the force in member 2 is zero, and member 1 carries the full load P.) Tj
T*
(   - Proof:) Tj
T*
(   Resolving perpendicular to member 1: F2 * sin\(theta\) = 0 => F2 = 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Structural Equilibrium & Kinematic Compatibility Check:) Tj
T*
(   - External determinacy verified via global equilibrium equations: Sigma Fx = 0, Sigma Fy = 0,) Tj
T*
(   Sigma M = 0.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
