(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze an equilateral triangular truss ABC of span 6 m \(sides 6 m\) supported by a hinge at A and roller at B, carrying a vertical load of 100 kN at apex C. Calculate all member forces using Method of Joints.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Context & Equilibrium Classification:) Tj
T*
(   This analysis addresses internal member forces and structural determinacy for plane truss) Tj
T*
(   systems.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria: All joints are frictionless spherical pins; loads act exclusively at nodes;) Tj
T*
(   members are ideal two-force axial elements carrying pure tension \(+T\) or compression \(-C\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation & Step-by-Step Joint/Section Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Complete Analysis of Equilateral Triangular Truss using Method of Joints:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometry and Global Equilibrium:) Tj
T*
(   Equilateral triangle ABC: Side lengths AB = BC = CA = 6.0 m.) Tj
T*
(   Interior angles: alpha = beta = gamma = 60 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   Height of apex C: h = 6 * sin\(60 deg\) = 6 * 0.8660 = 5.196 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical support reactions by symmetry:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma Fy = 0 => R_A + R_B = 100 kN.) Tj
T*
(   Sigma M_A = 0 => R_B * 6.0 - 100 * 3.0 = 0 => R_B = 50.0 kN \(upward\).) Tj
T*
(   R_A = 50.0 kN \(upward\). Horizontal reaction at hinge A: R_Ax = 0 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Equilibrium of Joint A:) Tj
T*
(   Forces acting at Joint A:) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction R_A = 50 kN upward \(+y\).) Tj
T*
(   - Member force F_AC directed along rafter AC at 60 deg to horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   - Member force F_AB directed along bottom chord AB horizontally \(+x\).) Tj
T*
(   Assume unknown forces F_AC and F_AB are in tension \(+\).) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical equilibrium: Sigma Fy = 0:) Tj
T*
(   R_A + F_AC * sin\(60 deg\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   50 + F_AC * \(0.8660\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   F_AC = - 50 / 0.8660 = - 57.74 kN.) Tj
T*
(   Negative sign indicates COMPRESSION: F_AC = 57.74 kN \(Compression\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal equilibrium: Sigma Fx = 0:) Tj
T*
(   F_AB + F_AC * cos\(60 deg\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   F_AB + \(- 57.74\) * 0.5000 = 0) Tj
T*
(   F_AB - 28.87 = 0 => F_AB = + 28.87 kN.) Tj
T*
(   Positive sign indicates TENSION: F_AB = 28.87 kN \(Tension\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
