/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A 6-bay Pratt truss of span 24 m \(panel width 4 m, height 4 m\) carries 80 kN loads at each bottom joint. Calculate the force in the center vertical member and diagonals.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Context & Equilibrium Classification:) Tj
T*
(   This analysis addresses internal member forces and structural determinacy for plane truss) Tj
T*
(   systems.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria: All joints are frictionless spherical pins; loads act exclusively at nodes;) Tj
T*
(   members are ideal two-force axial elements carrying pure tension \(+T\) or compression \(-C\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation & Step-by-Step Joint/Section Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Detailed Numerical Solution of 6-Bay Pratt Truss:) Tj
T*
(   1. Panel Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   Panels: 6 bays of 4 m = 24 m span. Height h = 4 m.) Tj
T*
(   Bottom joints: L0 to L6. Top joints: U1 to U5.) Tj
T*
(   Loads of 80 kN act at L1, L2, L3, L4, L5 \(5 loads\).) Tj
T*
(   Total downward load = 5 * 80 = 400 kN.) Tj
T*
(   Support reactions by symmetry: R_L0 = R_L6 = 200.0 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Web Diagonals \(Diagonal angle theta = 45 deg, sin\(45\) = cos\(45\) = 0.7071\):) Tj
T*
(   - Panel 1 \(End Post L0-U1\):) Tj
T*
(   Carries full shear V1 = 200 kN.) Tj
T*
(   F_{L0-U1} = 200 / sin\(45\) = 282.84 kN \(Compression\).) Tj
T*
(   - Panel 2 \(Diagonal L1-U2\):) Tj
T*
(   Carries shear V2 = 200 - 80 = 120 kN.) Tj
T*
(   F_{L1-U2} = 120 / sin\(45\) = 169.71 kN \(Tension\).) Tj
T*
(   - Panel 3 \(Diagonal L2-U3\):) Tj
T*
(   Carries shear V3 = 200 - 80 - 80 = 40 kN.) Tj
T*
(   F_{L2-U3} = 40 / sin\(45\) = 56.57 kN \(Tension\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Center Vertical Member U3-L3:) Tj
T*
(   Isolate joint L3:) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical downward load = 80 kN.) Tj
T*
