/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A planar roof truss carries wind loads perpendicular to the rafter. Formulate the method for computing horizontal and vertical reactions and joint equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Context & Equilibrium Classification:) Tj
T*
(   This analysis addresses internal member forces and structural determinacy for plane truss) Tj
T*
(   systems.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria: All joints are frictionless spherical pins; loads act exclusively at nodes;) Tj
T*
(   members are ideal two-force axial elements carrying pure tension \(+T\) or compression \(-C\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation & Step-by-Step Joint/Section Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Truss Analysis under Inclined Wind Loads:) Tj
T*
(   1. Nature of Wind Loads in Civil Engineering \(IS 875 Part 3\):) Tj
T*
(   Wind acts as aerodynamic pressure or suction perpendicular to the roof cladding slope) Tj
T*
(   \(rafters\):) Tj
T*
(   - Windward slope experiences normal pressure loads P_w perpendicular to rafter.) Tj
T*
(   - Leeward slope experiences aerodynamic suction \(negative pressure\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Global Equilibrium with One Roller Support:) Tj
T*
(   Let left support A be a fixed hinge and right support B be on horizontal rollers:) Tj
T*
(   - Right support B reaction R_B MUST be purely vertical \(R_Bx = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Moments about Hinge A \(Sigma M_A = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Includes moments of all perpendicular wind forces P_w * d_i:) Tj
T*
(   R_B * Span - Sigma \( P_wi * d_i \) = 0 => Solves R_B.) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal equilibrium: Sigma Fx = 0:) Tj
T*
(   R_Ax + Sigma \( P_wi * sin\(theta_slope\) \) = 0 => Solves horizontal hinge thrust R_Ax.) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical equilibrium: Sigma Fy = 0:) Tj
T*
(   R_Ay + R_B - Sigma \( P_wi * cos\(theta_slope\) \) = 0 => Solves R_Ay.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Joint Equilibrium:) Tj
T*
(   At each joint, the inclined wind load is added as an external active vector in the joint FBD) Tj
T*
(   equations: Sigma Fx = 0 and Sigma Fy = 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Structural Equilibrium & Kinematic Compatibility Check:) Tj
T*
(   - External determinacy verified via global equilibrium equations: Sigma Fx = 0, Sigma Fy = 0,) Tj
T*
ET

