/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A planar truss has 6 joints and 9 members. Prove whether it is internally determinate, redundant, or deficient.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Context & Equilibrium Classification:) Tj
T*
(   This analysis addresses internal member forces and structural determinacy for plane truss) Tj
T*
(   systems.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria: All joints are frictionless spherical pins; loads act exclusively at nodes;) Tj
T*
(   members are ideal two-force axial elements carrying pure tension \(+T\) or compression \(-C\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation & Step-by-Step Joint/Section Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Internal Determinacy Proof:) Tj
T*
(   Formula: m = 2 * j - 3.) Tj
T*
(   Given: j = 6 joints, m = 9 members.) Tj
T*
(   Required for perfect truss: m_req = 2 * 6 - 3 = 12 - 3 = 9 members.) Tj
T*
(   Since actual members m \(9\) = required members m_req \(9\):) Tj
T*
(   The truss is perfectly Statically Determinate and rigid. \(Proved\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Structural Equilibrium & Kinematic Compatibility Check:) Tj
T*
(   - External determinacy verified via global equilibrium equations: Sigma Fx = 0, Sigma Fy = 0,) Tj
T*
(   Sigma M = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Internal determinacy satisfied via Maxwell's criterion: m = 2*j - 3.) Tj
T*
(   - Joint node equilibrium confirmed: Vector resultant of all concurrent member forces vanishes) Tj
T*
(   at each pin.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Civil Engineering Design & Stability Implications:) Tj
T*
(   Compression members must be checked for Euler column buckling \(P_cr = pi^2 * E * I / L_eff^2\),) Tj
T*
(   while tension members are governed by net cross-sectional yield strength under bridge/roof) Tj
T*
(   design standards.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
