(   [Problem Statement]: Summarize the complete structural design workflow for civil engineering roof and bridge trusses.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Context & Equilibrium Classification:) Tj
T*
(   This analysis addresses internal member forces and structural determinacy for plane truss) Tj
T*
(   systems.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria: All joints are frictionless spherical pins; loads act exclusively at nodes;) Tj
T*
(   members are ideal two-force axial elements carrying pure tension \(+T\) or compression \(-C\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation & Step-by-Step Joint/Section Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Civil Engineering Truss Design Workflow:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architectural Span and Pitch Selection: Choose truss profile \(Pratt, Warren, Fink\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Load Computation: Dead load \(cladding, purlins\), Live load \(occupancy/traffic\),) Tj
T*
(   Wind/Earthquake loads \(IS 875/893\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Structural Modeling: Analyze member axial forces using Method of Joints/Sections or) Tj
T*
(   stiffness matrix software.) Tj
T*
(   4. Load Combinations and Stress Envelope: Find maximum tension and compression for each member.) Tj
T*
